1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,220
This diamond is on fire, and it's turning into thin air.

2
00:00:03,799 --> 00:00:06,960
A diamond is pure carbon, just like charcoal.

3
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:10,759
Heat it to about 1,500 degrees in pure oxygen, and it burns.

4
00:00:11,480 --> 00:00:15,039
Every atom flies off as carbon dioxide, the gas you breathe out.

5
00:00:15,419 --> 00:00:18,980
Even in a ring, every diamond is slowly turning into pencil lead.

6
00:00:19,339 --> 00:00:21,120
Just way too slowly to ever see.

7
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:23,500
So diamonds aren't forever. look.
